---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Chat with My Research | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="A citation-first agentic RAG project for querying a local research corpus with evidence-linked answers."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<p>OPEN-SOURCE PROJECT · AGENTIC RAG · CITATIONS</p>
			<h1>Chat with My Research</h1>
			<p>
				Ask questions across a research corpus and inspect the
				passages behind every answer. Its MCTS extension searches
				multi-hop decomposition trees with UCT, retrieval-confidence
				pruning, and an evidence value function.
			</p>

			<section aria-labelledby="workflow">
				<h2 id="workflow">Follow the evidence</h2>
				<ol>
					<li>Plan focused queries, preserving the original question.</li>
					<li>Retrieve relevant passages from the local SQLite FTS index.</li>
					<li>Optionally rerank passages with Cohere.</li>
					<li>Answer with source citations—or show an extractive preview without model credentials.</li>
				</ol>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="search">
				<h2 id="search">Compare planning strategies</h2>
				<p>
					Compare MCTS, an admissible A* retrieval-cost variant,
					and beam search against Self-Ask, least-to-most, linear,
					and ReAct-style baselines. Inspect the bounded search
					tree and plot labeled multi-hop source accuracy against
					retrieval calls.
				</p>
				<p>
					The A* heuristic uses a zero lower bound on remaining
					non-negative call cost; normalized retrieval confidence
					breaks ties. Confidence and the default value function are
					lexical estimates, not calibrated probabilities or
					answer-correctness guarantees.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="demo">
				<h2 id="demo">Try the local demo</h2>
				<pre><code>cd chat-with-my-research
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
research-chat ingest data/demo-corpus
streamlit run dashboard.py</code></pre>
				<p>
					The included notes are synthetic project fixtures, not
					representations of my papers, talks, or personal views.
					Add your own authorized corpus locally; the index is
					git-ignored by default. Without an API key, the demo
					shows extractive passages and makes no model-provider calls.
				</p>
				<p>
					Run the strategy comparison from the dashboard, or use
					<code>research-chat compare --dataset samples/evaluation.jsonl</code>.
					The sample scores are synthetic demonstration data, not
					published benchmark results.
				</p>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="questions">
				<h2 id="questions">Example questions</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>What does the sample note say about agent autonomy?</li>
					<li>Compare evaluation to observability.</li>
					<li>Which sample passage discusses tracing answers to sources?</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					Source-level metrics include recall@k, precision@k,
					reciprocal rank, citation precision, unsupported
					citations, and optional required-term coverage.
				</p>
				<p><a href="/">Back to profile</a></p>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
